CORE
unknown.c
--stop-on-fail --sarif-result -
activate-multi-line-match
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
"ruleId": "main\.assertion\.1"
"kind": "open"
"level": "warning"
"ruleId": "main\.assertion\.2"
"kind": "fail"
"level": "error"
--
--
Checks the UNKNOWN -> open/warning SARIF mapping: under --stop-on-fail an
undecided property is reported with kind "open" and level "warning", while the
failing property is reported with kind "fail" and level "error".
